**Fix:** Guard the membership test with `try/except TypeError`. If `obj` is unhashable, it definitionally cannot be one of the pre-registered builtin type constructors (all of which are hashable), so we safely treat it as not special-cased and fall through to the normal function-pickling path:

```python
